uilt-in tool that acts as the owner to the connector rule\n\nRound 1 found that a tool built into the agent CLI which acts through the\nowner's own sessions, such as a browser integration, was deemed declared and so\nescaped the \"never\". The owner's O25 counts such a tool like a connector. What\ncounts as declared now turns on three conditions, so R-SAFE-7 becomes a lead row\nwith continuation rows R-SAFE-8 and R-SAFE-9.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0113bpZDJ6DYsJNYwDpFzafi","tree":{"sha":"1970eecf498930b07470d122a416f1c57afe910f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/git/trees/1970eecf498930b07470d122a416f1c57afe910f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/git/commits/f365b232434c9f3b47c82b26e12ba98626a65a5d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/commits/f365b232434c9f3b47c82b26e12ba98626a65a5d","html_url":"https://github.com/williacj/rigger/commit/f365b232434c9f3b47c82b26e12ba98626a65a5d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/commits/f365b232434c9f3b47c82b26e12ba98626a65a5d/comments","author":{"login":"williacj","id":121251353,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzomGQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121251353?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj","html_url":"https://github.com/williacj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"williacj","id":121251353,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzomGQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121251353?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj","html_url":"https://github.com/williacj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e7db75196962d19494c2fddae2f53a7cce135a01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/commits/e7db75196962d19494c2fddae2f53a7cce135a01","html_url":"https://github.com/williacj/rigger/commit/e7db75196962d19494c2fddae2f53a7cce135a01"}]},{"sha":"559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc","node_id":"C_kwDOTcdlStoAKDU1OWRiNWJmODNmNGI3YzMwYzEwOThiYTQ5NDQ4NzUzNDNhZjcyY2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"CJ Williams","email":"121251353+williacj@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-01T15:13:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"CJ Williams","email":"121251353+williacj@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-01T15:13:00Z"},"message":"Read R-SAFE-9's tools that act as the owner as examples\n\nThe sentence naming a browser, the desktop and publishing as the owner read as\na closed definition. The owner's O28 has it read as examples, as O25's \"e.g.\"\ndid, so a built-in tool acting through the owner's sessions some other way is\nstill held to the repository's declaration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0113bpZDJ6DYsJNYwDpFzafi","tree":{"sha":"5a76fbc5bd94c580104000980874d6d701f0e957","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/git/trees/5a76fbc5bd94c580104000980874d6d701f0e957"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/git/commits/559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/commits/559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc","html_url":"https://github.com/williacj/rigger/commit/559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/commits/559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc/comments","author":{"login":"williacj","id":121251353,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzomGQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121251353?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj","html_url":"https://github.com/williacj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"williacj","id":121251353,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzomGQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121251353?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj","html_url":"https://github.com/williacj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williacj/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f365b232434c9f3b47c82b26e12ba98626a65a5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/commits/f365b232434c9f3b47c82b26e12ba98626a65a5d","html_url":"https://github.com/williacj/rigger/commit/f365b232434c9f3b47c82b26e12ba98626a65a5d"}]}],"files":[{"sha":"188fc54cc6e5f5af5632498804e2b582d04ec0e5","filename":"docs/derived/test-matrix.md","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0,"changes":3,"blob_url":"https://github.com/williacj/rigger/blob/559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc/docs%2Fderived%2Ftest-matrix.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/williacj/rigger/raw/559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc/docs%2Fderived%2Ftest-matrix.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/contents/docs%2Fderived%2Ftest-matrix.md?ref=559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc","patch":"@@ -163,4 +163,7 @@ reports no gap of its own; the register carries the reason.\n | R-SAFE-4 | **gap** |\n | R-SAFE-5 | `test/doctor.test.mjs` doctor refuses the source tree it is running from, and asks nothing before it does<br>`test/doctor.test.mjs` a worktree beside the source tree is not the source tree, however its name begins<br>`test/doctor.test.mjs` a second spelling of the source tree is still the source tree<br>`test/doctor.test.mjs` the tree compared is the repository, not the directory the command was run in<br>`test/doctor.test.mjs` a tree git cannot name is refused rather than compared against the working directory<br>`test/guard-probe-kill.test.mjs` given a git stand-in for the guard that leaves a child alive, and a target that is Rigger's own source tree, the kill is reported on standard error, naming the process name and command line, and the target's git status is unchanged<br>`test/guard-probe-kill.test.mjs` given a git stand-in for the guard that leaves a child alive, and a target that is no repository, the kill is reported on standard error, and nothing is written under the target<br>`test/init.test.mjs` given a target that is the running package's source tree, init exits non-zero naming R-SAFE-5, asks git nothing, and leaves the tree's git status as it was<br>`test/once.test.mjs` once run against the source tree it is running from exits non-zero, names R-SAFE-5, and claims nothing<br>`test/package.test.mjs` the installed rigger init, run against a target inside the installed package, exits non-zero naming R-SAFE-5, asks git nothing, and changes no file under the package<br>`test/package.test.mjs` the installed rigger init, run against the target whose node_modules it is installed under, exits non-zero naming R-SAFE-5, asks git nothing, and changes no file under the target<br>`test/plan.test.mjs` plan run against the source tree it is running from exits non-zero, names R-SAFE-5, and reads no board<br>`test/report.test.mjs` report run against the source tree it is running from exits non-zero and names R-SAFE-5<br>`test/run.test.mjs` run run against the source tree it is running from exits non-zero, names R-SAFE-5, and claims nothing<br>`test/setup-board.test.mjs` setup-board run against the source tree it is running from exits non-zero, names R-SAFE-5, and writes nothing<br>`test/verbs-provision.test.mjs` given a worktree root inside the running package's source tree, rigger once exits non-zero naming R-SAFE-5 before it claims any card<br>`test/verbs-provision.test.mjs` given a worktree root inside the running package's source tree, rigger once creates nothing under the running package's source tree<br>`test/verbs-provision.test.mjs` given a worktree root inside the running package's source tree, rigger run exits non-zero naming R-SAFE-5 before it claims any card<br>`test/verbs-provision.test.mjs` given a worktree root inside the running package's source tree, rigger run creates nothing under the running package's source tree |\n | R-SAFE-6 | `test/init.test.mjs` every role the written config names reads its prompt out of the consumer repository<br>`test/init.test.mjs` the command forks the assets into the repository it is run in, from the package alone |\n+| R-SAFE-7 | **gap** |\n+| R-SAFE-8 | **gap** |\n+| R-SAFE-9 | **gap** |\n | R-OPTION-1 | **gap** |"},{"sha":"e0da9bd1965e43e57f2ec6ab3cafbf2b2030ee5d","filename":"docs/journal/2026-10-01-0838-357-declared-tools.md","status":"added","additions":30,"deletions":0,"changes":30,"blob_url":"https://github.com/williacj/rigger/blob/559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc/docs%2Fjournal%2F2026-10-01-0838-357-declared-tools.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/williacj/rigger/raw/559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc/docs%2Fjournal%2F2026-10-01-0838-357-declared-tools.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/contents/docs%2Fjournal%2F2026-10-01-0838-357-declared-tools.md?ref=559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+ABOUTME: Journal for #357: proposing R-SAFE-7 to R-SAFE-9, that a dispatched agent uses only the\n+tools and connectors the consumer's repository declares, and the two words the rows had to define.\n+\n+# #357 — what a dispatched agent may reach is the repository's to say\n+\n+**The need came from a spike, not a failure.** The M2-S1 spike's headless Claude Code runs\n+connected the owner's claude.ai Gmail and Shopify connectors in every run\n+(`docs/spikes/what-leaves-the-process-group.md`, \"The MCP servers it declared\"). No maker has used\n+one. The owner ruled that a dispatched agent may use only what the consumer's repository declares\n+(\"Spike #355 findings\", on #332).\n+\n+**\"Tools\" already meant something else in the register.** `R-SAFE-1` and `R-SAFE-2` use it for the\n+programs Rigger itself calls. So the new row scopes the word to itself, as an action the agent CLI\n+offers the agent. \"Connector\" appears in no binding document, so the row defines it too.\n+\n+**The card's words left the built-in tools to a guess.** None of this repository's role prompts\n+lists a tool, so read strictly, the card's row would leave a maker no shell and no editor. The row\n+counts each built-in tool as declared unless the repository withholds it.\n+\n+**A built-in tool can be a connector in all but name.** Two round-1 judges found the gap: Claude\n+Code's browser integration and Codex's browser and computer-use features ship with the CLI and act\n+through the owner's signed-in sessions. Deemed declared, they escaped the \"never\". The owner's O25\n+(on #357) counts such a tool like a connector: never used unless the repository declares it. The\n+row became a lead row and two continuation rows, `R-SAFE-7` to `R-SAFE-9`, because what counts as\n+declared now turns on three conditions.\n+\n+**What the rows do not reach.** Skills and hooks in the owner's own account load into a dispatched\n+session too: the session that wrote these rows was offered the owner's personal skills. Those are\n+`R-SAFE-6`'s, under architect rulings 1 (Q1) and 4 on #467, so these rows leave them alone. A\n+plugin's tools and connectors are within them."},{"sha":"ef415d92b7dac935bab7210fd664b1d820c57761","filename":"docs/spec/requirements.md","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0,"changes":3,"blob_url":"https://github.com/williacj/rigger/blob/559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc/docs%2Fspec%2Frequirements.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/williacj/rigger/raw/559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc/docs%2Fspec%2Frequirements.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/williacj/rigger/contents/docs%2Fspec%2Frequirements.md?ref=559db5bf83f4b7c30c1098ba4944875343af72cc","patch":"@@ -294,6 +294,9 @@ reads both files. A group with no requirements yet is not written until it has o\n | R-SAFE-4 | An agent Rigger dispatches has the access of the account Rigger runs under, and no more. | the operating system | the operating system | |\n | R-SAFE-5 | Rigger never runs against the source tree it is running from. | the engine | the test suite | |\n | R-SAFE-6 | The role prompts, skills and hooks a consumer uses live in the consumer's repository. Rigger reads none of them from its own package at run time. | the engine | the test suite | |\n+| R-SAFE-7 | An agent Rigger dispatches can use only the tools and connectors the consumer's repository declares. A tool in these rows is an action the agent CLI offers the agent. A connector is an outside service, such as mail or a shop, that the agent acts on through the owner's own sessions or login. What counts as declared: | the engine | the test suite | |\n+| R-SAFE-8 | — a tool built into the agent CLI counts as declared unless the repository withholds it, except a tool `R-SAFE-9` names; | the engine | the test suite | |\n+| R-SAFE-9 | — a connector, and a built-in tool that acts through the owner's own sessions or login, count as declared only where the repository declares them. Such a tool, for example, drives the owner's browser or desktop, or publishes as the owner. The agent never uses one the repository does not declare, even a connector the owner connected to their own account. | the engine | the test suite | |\n \n ## R-OPTION — what a consumer may leave out\n "}]}